1 | devops | READ-ONLY REVIEW of PR 2721, branch ci/e2e-aptget-hang. You are not a producer: no commits, no push, no gh pr review, no gh pr merge, no labels. Permitted writes are a /tmp worktree only. Record the PR head SHA at start and re-check at report. TWO FILES: .github/workflows/ci.yml and a new scripts/ci/install-playwright-deps.sh. WHAT IT CLAIMS TO DO: split the Playwright browser download from the apt-get OS-deps install, make the download fatal with a 4-minute step cap, make the apt step bounded and NON-FATAL, and remove --with-deps so an apt stall can no longer cancel the step that must succeed. THE ONE THING THAT MATTERS MOST: verify a stalled or failing apt can no longer cancel the job or skip the tests. Read the new script and the step wiring and answer concretely — if apt hangs, what happens; if apt exits non-zero, what happens; does the E2E test step still run in both cases. A fix that merely moves the stall to a different step has not fixed anything. SECOND: the job keeps timeout-minutes 12 and the surrounding comment says twice that it must NOT be raised. Confirm it was not raised, and that the new step-level caps genuinely fit inside it alongside the lane 5-minute test budget rather than merely appearing to. THIRD: the PR asserts, as MEASURED not assumed, that the previous comment claiming OS libs MUST be reinstalled on every cache hit was false — that on job 95890668237 every library chromium links against already reported is already the newest version, and only 9 font packages actually install. Verify that claim rather than accepting it, because the whole design rests on it: if those libs really are needed, making the step non-fatal would let tests run against a broken browser and fail confusingly instead of cleanly. FOURTH: the diff adds scripts/ci/** to the ci_workflows path filter so a PR touching only the helper still runs the job. Confirm that filter change cannot accidentally widen or narrow which jobs run for unrelated paths. FIFTH: confirm non-fatal really means non-fatal in the shell sense — no set -e interaction, no masked exit code that would make a genuine tooling failure look like success forever. Do NOT re-litigate anything outside these two files. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC PR 2721, with a verdict of SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE and file:line citations. No vendor names, emails, booking ids or gcloud payloads. | ci/e2e-aptget-hang
